---
description: Common rules for data types and Zod schemas across all projects
globs: 
alwaysApply: true
---
- All shared types and Zod schemas should be defined in `*/lib/definitions.ts` (e.g., `astro-app/src/lib/definitions.ts` or `next-app/lib/definitions.ts`)
- Import types using: `import type { TypeName } from '@/lib/definitions'`
- Types are inferred from Zod schemas using `z.infer<typeof SchemaZ>`
- Always use shared types instead of defining duplicate types
- When adding new types, add Zod schemas first, then export the inferred TypeScript types
- Use `@/` alias for imports (configured in tsconfig.json)

**Astro App Types:**
- Available types include: `UserType`, `MatchupType`, `PickType`, `ScoreboardType`, `StatType`, `WeeklyStatType`, `GameType`, `PageEntryType`, `MatchupsByCodePrefixType`, `ReactionType`, `UserSettingsType`
- Location: `astro-app/src/lib/definitions.ts`
- [Astro definitions.ts](mdc:astro-app/src/lib/definitions.ts)

**Next.js App Types:**
- Available types include: `UserType`, `UserSettingsType` (and others as they're added)
- Server Actions should export their own state types (e.g., `LoginFormState`, `SignupFormState`)
- Location: `next-app/lib/definitions.ts`
- [Next.js definitions.ts](mdc:next-app/lib/definitions.ts)
